-1. Add the `DebugBridge` SPM dependency to the app's `Package.swift`. The package
-   ships three Debug-config-only library products:
+1. Generate the local `DebugBridge` package from the shipped templates. There
+   is NO published DebugBridge package to depend on — the package is rendered
+   into the app's repo (e.g. `<app-repo>/DebugBridge/`). Copy each file from
+   `$GSTACK_ROOT/ios-qa/templates/`, dropping the `.template` suffix:
+   - `Package.swift.template` → `DebugBridge/Package.swift`
+   - `StateServer.swift.template`, `DebugBridgeManager.swift.template`
+     → `DebugBridge/Sources/DebugBridgeCore/`
+   - `DebugBridgeTouch.h.template`
+     → `DebugBridge/Sources/DebugBridgeTouch/include/DebugBridgeTouch.h`
+   - `DebugBridgeTouch.m.template`
+     → `DebugBridge/Sources/DebugBridgeTouch/DebugBridgeTouch.m`
+   - `Bridges.swift.template`, `DebugOverlay.swift.template`
+     → `DebugBridge/Sources/DebugBridgeUI/`
+   Then add it to the app as a LOCAL package dependency:
+   `.package(path: "DebugBridge")` in the app's `Package.swift` (or Xcode →
+   File → Add Package Dependencies → Add Local). The package ships three
+   Debug-config-only library products:
    - `DebugBridgeCore` (Swift, cross-platform) — StateServer + bridge protocols.
    - `DebugBridgeTouch` (Objective-C, iOS-only) — KIF-derived in-process touch
      synthesis with iOS 18+ `_UIHitTestContext` SwiftUI hit-testing.
